{"sourceSha256": "bf4eb1acd6c47c648a3d79fdd3d5a3ccc5b0ea24fbdc400634c9ffaa478e620c", "text": "Dear Dr. Smile,\nRe: Ruth Devotch, D.O.B. 12/06/2009\n\n| am referring this young girl for an opinion on her thyroid tssues. Ruth's past history\nincludes eczema, which ts controlled by vanious treatment. She is the youngest of three\nchildren. Her older sister also has eczema as well as asthma. Although there is no family\nhistory of thyroid problems, there is autoimmune history on the paternal side of the family\n\nRuth was noted to have increased swelling in her neck in late 2018. Since then Ruth has\ndeveloped mild symptoms of thyroid dysfunction. Her limbs tend to feel cold and she has\nsome intermittent lethargy. She has had long standing constipation which improved with\ndietary modification. Repeated ultrasound testing has shown the ongoing presence of\nthyroglossal cysts and increased vascularity of the gland. Her recent thyroid function test\nrevealed a slight increase of TSH while her T4 remains normal. Please note, there was\nsignificant elevation of her antithyroid antibodies in 2018.\n\nOn today’s examination, Ruth is well, and growing at 143.9om with a weight of 35 kg. Her\nheart rate was 76 anc blood pressure was normal at 110/60. She had a very mild goiter\nwhich was smooth on palpation and there was no associated lymphadenopathy. Reflexes\n\nwere normal.\n\nIn my opinion, at this stage monitoring of thyroid function is required and your advice on\n\nfurther management of this case would be gratefully appreciated.\nYours sincerely,\n\nDr. Vera Mice", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "Dear Dr. Smile,\nRe: Ruth Devotch, D.O.B. 12/06/2009\n\n| am referring this young girl for an opinion on her thyroid tssues. Ruth's past history\nincludes eczema, which ts controlled by vanious treatment. She is the youngest of three\nchildren. Her older sister also has eczema as well as asthma. Although there is no family\nhistory of thyroid problems, there is autoimmune history on the paternal side of the family\n\nRuth was noted to have increased swelling in her neck in late 2018. Since then Ruth has\ndeveloped mild symptoms of thyroid dysfunction. Her limbs tend to feel cold and she has\nsome intermittent lethargy. She has had long standing constipation which improved with\ndietary modification. Repeated ultrasound testing has shown the ongoing presence of\nthyroglossal cysts and increased vascularity of the gland. Her recent thyroid function test\nrevealed a slight increase of TSH while her T4 remains normal. Please note, there was\nsignificant elevation of her antithyroid antibodies in 2018.\n\nOn today’s examination, Ruth is well, and growing at 143.9om with a weight of 35 kg. Her\nheart rate was 76 anc blood pressure was normal at 110/60. She had a very mild goiter\nwhich was smooth on palpation and there was no associated lymphadenopathy. Reflexes\n\nwere normal.\n\nIn my opinion, at this stage monitoring of thyroid function is required and your advice on\n\nfurther management of this case would be gratefully appreciated.\nYours sincerely,\n\nDr. Vera Mice", "extraction": "ocr", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 2333.0, "height": 2800.0, "blocks": [{"text": "Dear Dr. Smile,\nRe: Ruth Devotch, D.O.B. 12/06/2009", "lines": [{"text": "Dear Dr. Smile,", "x": 0.01414, "y": 0.01429, "width": 0.15902, "height": 0.01893, "confidence": 0.942, "words": [{"text": "Dear", "x": 0.01414, "width": 0.05015, "confidence": 0.961}, {"text": "Dr.", "x": 0.07115, "width": 0.02743, "confidence": 0.905}, {"text": "Smile,", "x": 0.10673, "width": 0.06644, "confidence": 0.959}], "uncertainWords": []}, {"text": "Re: Ruth Devotch, D.O.B. 12/06/2009", "x": 0.01414, "y": 0.0575, "width": 0.40592, "height": 0.01893, "confidence": 0.909, "words": [{"text": "Re:", "x": 0.01414, "width": 0.03258, "confidence": 0.962}, {"text": "Ruth", "x": 0.05615, "width": 0.04758, "confidence": 0.904}, {"text": "Devotch,", "x": 0.11273, "width": 0.09301, "confidence": 0.904}, {